    <item>
      <title>Property Changes</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/dev/tech/properties/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/dev/tech/properties/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Recommended reading:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;The Application Module&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://wiki.freecad.org/Property&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;Property in the wiki&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2&#xA;  id=&#34;the-app-side&#34;&gt;&#xA;  The App side&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34;&#xA;     href=&#34;#the-app-side&#34;&#xA;     title=&#34;The App side&#34;&#xA;     aria-label=&#34;The App side&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;icon-anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M15 7h3a5 5 0 015 5 5 5 0 01-5 5h-3m-6 0H6a5 5 0 01-5-5 5 5 0 015-5h3&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;8&#34; y1=&#34;12&#34; x2=&#34;16&#34; y2=&#34;12&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;When a Property&amp;rsquo;s value changes, its PropertyContainer (eventually a DocumentObject) executes the onChanged method with the Property as a parameter.  This is where you will take appropriate action based on the new property value.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Be cautious when inserting logic into onChanged and execute as it is possible to create a loop.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;codeblock&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-c++&#34; data-lang=&#34;c++&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;kt&#34;&gt;void&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;myFeature&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;execute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;    &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;MyProperty&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;setValue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;foo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;());&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;kt&#34;&gt;void&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;myFeature&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;onChanged&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;App&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;Property&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;property&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;    &lt;span class=&#34;k&#34;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;property&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;MyProperty&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;        &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;execute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;    &lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;The other interesting method involving property changes is mustExecute.   This is where you control whether or not your object participates in the next recompute cycle.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2&#xA;  id=&#34;the-gui-side&#34;&gt;&#xA;  The Gui side&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34;&#xA;     href=&#34;#the-gui-side&#34;&#xA;     title=&#34;The Gui side&#34;&#xA;     aria-label=&#34;The Gui side&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;icon-anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M15 7h3a5 5 0 015 5 5 5 0 01-5 5h-3m-6 0H6a5 5 0 01-5-5 5 5 0 015-5h3&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;8&#34; y1=&#34;12&#34; x2=&#34;16&#34; y2=&#34;12&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;On the Gui side, we must look first at your derived ViewProvider, which is attached to your DocumentObject.  The ViewProvider is notified of changed properties for both itself and the DocumentObject it belongs to.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;For properties belonging to the ViewProvider (those on the View tab in the PropertyEditor), the relevant method is again onChanged.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Whenever a DocumentObject Property changes, the updateData method of its attached ViewProvider is called.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Python Binding</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/dev/tech/python-binding/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/dev/tech/python-binding/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2&#xA;  id=&#34;background&#34;&gt;&#xA;  Background&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34;&#xA;     href=&#34;#background&#34;&#xA;     title=&#34;Background&#34;&#xA;     aria-label=&#34;Background&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;icon-anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M15 7h3a5 5 0 015 5 5 5 0 01-5 5h-3m-6 0H6a5 5 0 01-5-5 5 5 0 015-5h3&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;8&#34; y1=&#34;12&#34; x2=&#34;16&#34; y2=&#34;12&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;It becomes necessary at times to expand the FreeCAD API further by exposing functions that are available in the source code in c++ to the python. This process is generally referred to as creating a binding.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Python stubs</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/dev/tech/python-stubs/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/dev/tech/python-stubs/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Python is a dynamically typed language, so there is no error when compiling&#xA;(Yes, Python can compile).&#xA;Compiling/interpreting is an abstract concept, language independent.&#xA;See more on &lt;a href=&#34;https://stackoverflow.com/a/6889798&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;stackoverflow&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;).&#xA;Instead, an error is reported at runtime&#xA;which may significantly slow down developing process.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
