    <item>
      <title>Release Process</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/dev/tech/release/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/dev/tech/release/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;We recognize signficant wisdom in the philosophy to &lt;a href=&#34;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Release_early,_release_often&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;&amp;ldquo;Release Early and Release Often&amp;rdquo;&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. However, releases can require significant coordinated work within the community.  FreeCAD aspires to produce a major release every 3-6 months. In order to meet this goal, we will work to make releases more predicatable and automated.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Snap package</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/dev/tech/snap/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/dev/tech/snap/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;FreeCAD is provided as a Snap package in multiple versions:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;stable &amp;ndash; built from the latest full release&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;beta &amp;ndash; built weekly from master&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;edge &amp;ndash; built daily from master&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;freecad-realthunder &amp;ndash; a convenience build of the LinkStage3 branch&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Each of these is represented by a branch at &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/FreeCAD/FreeCAD-snap&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;https://github.com/FreeCAD/FreeCAD-snap&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &amp;ndash; to make changes,edit &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/FreeCAD/FreeCAD-snap/blob/master/snap/snapcraft.yaml&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;the snapcraft.yaml file&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; on the branch you want to update.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Source Tree</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/dev/tech/src/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/dev/tech/src/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The full FreeCAD source tree has many other branches, but most Contributors will&#xA;only need to deal with these:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;figure&gt;&#xA;        &lt;img src=&#34;https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/dev/tech/src/sourcetreebasics.svg&#34;&#xA;          title=&#34;The FreeCAD Source Tree&#34;&#xA;          alt=&#34;The FreeCAD Source Tree&#34;&#xA;          loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xA;          fetchpriority=&#34;low&#34;&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;The FreeCAD Source Tree&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;codeblock&#34;&gt;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;graph LR&#xA;    A[src] --- B[App: Documents, DocumentObjects, EventPropagation]&#xA;    A --- C[Base: FundamentalTypes, Utilities]&#xA;    A --- D[Gui: Windows, Menus, Dialogs]&#xA;    A --- E[Mod: ApplicationLogic]&#xA;    subgraph Mod: ApplicationLogic&#xA;    E[Mod] --- F[Arch: Buildings]&#xA;    E --- G[Draft: 2DDesign]&#xA;    E --- H[Part: BasicShapes, BooleanOps]&#xA;    E --- I[&amp;#34;...&amp;#34;]&#xA;    end&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Windows LibPack</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/dev/tech/libpack/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/dev/tech/libpack/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;To create a new LibPack for Windows, begin by creating an empty directory. The suggested naming scheme&#xA;is to name it &amp;ldquo;LibPack-XX-YY-ARCH&amp;rdquo; where XX is the release of FreeCAD the pack is intended to work with,&#xA;YY is a version number of the LibPack itself, and ARCH is the architecture the LibPack was build for&#xA;(e.g. x86_64 or arm64). The rest of this document will refer to that directory as &lt;em&gt;LIBPACK&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
  </channel>
